To solve the task of checking if a specific cell in an Excel file contains either "0" or "1" using C++, Qt, and the QXlsx library, you'll first need to set up a Qt project and integrate the QXlsx library.

### Step 1: Setup Qt Environment and QXlsx Library

1. **Install Qt**: Download and install Qt from the [Qt website](https://www.qt.io/download) if you haven't already. Make sure to include the Qt Creator IDE in your installation.

2. **Download and Integrate QXlsx**:
   - Clone or download the QXlsx source code from its repository (https://github.com/QtExcel/QXlsx).
